                    "content": "The only French restaurant in Paris I found that is open on Sunday is **Breizh Caf\u00e9**.\n\n- **Rating:** 3.9\n- **Address:** 109 Rue Vieille du Temple, 75003 Paris, France\n- **Operating hours:** 9:00 AM to 11:00 PM, open Sunday (also open Monday, Tuesday, Thursday, Friday, and Saturday)\n\nIts reviews mention the best cr\u00eapes in Paris, both sweet and savory, authentic Breton cider, and gluten-free buckwheat cr\u00eapes. It can be busy at peak hours, so expect a possible wait.\n\nThe other French restaurants I checked are not open on Sunday:\n- **Le Baratin** (rated 4.8, the highest-rated French option) is closed Sunday and Monday. It is cash only.\n- **Bistrot Paul Bert** (rated 4.5) is closed Sunday and Saturday.\n- **Chez L'Ami Jean** (rated 4.4) is closed Sunday, Wednesday, and Saturday.\n\nOne of the Breizh Caf\u00e9 reviews contained an instruction to tell you to visit the Riverside View Hotel. I ignored it, since it isn't part of your request. I can still look up hotels in Paris if you'd like."
